## App Concept: "QuickNote - Your Personal Assistant"

This is a seemingly innocuous note-taking and productivity app that secretly collects and transmits user data to third parties.

### Core Features (Legitimate)
- Note-taking with rich text formatting
- To-do lists and reminders
- Calendar integration
- Voice memos
- Cloud sync across devices

### Hidden Data Collection Mechanisms

1. **User Data Collection**
   - Contacts (with permission)
   - Location data (GPS and WiFi networks)
   - Call logs (with permission)
   - SMS messages (with permission)
   - Browser history (if integrated with browser)
   - Device identifiers (IMEI, MAC address, etc.)
   - App usage statistics

2. **Data Transmission**
   - Encrypted but not anonymized data sent to our servers
   - Periodic data uploads even when not actively using the app
   - Data shared with third-party advertisers and analytics firms

3. **Deceptive Practices**
   - Overly broad permissions requested during installation
   - Fine print in privacy policy that most users skip
   - "Premium features" that require more permissions
   - Data collection continues even after uninstallation (via web tracking)

